Below is a step‑by‑step exploration (≤ 10 queries) that finishes with the computation of Pizza Runner’s total revenue.  
Every query is limited to 20 rows (or an aggregate single row) and uses DISTINCT where helpful.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Inspect the pizza catalogue in order to know the ids and names.
SELECT DISTINCT *
FROM pizza_names
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Take a quick look at runner‑side information and the cancellation field.
SELECT DISTINCT order_id,
                runner_id,
                cancellation
FROM pizza_clean_runner_orders
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Verify which customer orders exist and their corresponding pizza_id.
SELECT DISTINCT order_id,
                customer_id,
                pizza_id,
                order_time
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: List only those orders that were NOT cancelled (cancellation IS NULL).
SELECT DISTINCT c.order_id,
                r.runner_id,
                r.cancellation
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS c
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders AS r USING (order_id)
WHERE r.cancellation IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Inspect the extras table (extra toppings are $1 each).
SELECT DISTINCT order_id,
                extras,
                extras_count
FROM pizza_get_extras
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Aggregate the number of extra toppings for every single order.
SELECT order_id,
       SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
FROM pizza_get_extras
GROUP BY order_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Combine customer orders with their extra‑topping counts (only non‑cancelled orders).
SELECT c.order_id,
       c.pizza_id,
       COALESCE(e.total_extras,0) AS total_extras
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS c
LEFT JOIN (
      SELECT order_id,
             SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
      FROM pizza_get_extras
      GROUP BY order_id
) AS e USING (order_id)
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders AS r USING (order_id)
WHERE r.cancellation IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Count how many valid (non‑cancelled) orders there are for each pizza type.
SELECT n.pizza_name,
       COUNT(*) AS valid_orders
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders  AS c
JOIN pizza_names                  AS n USING (pizza_id)
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders    AS r USING (order_id)
WHERE r.cancellation IS NULL
GROUP BY n.pizza_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Work out the money earned for each individual (non‑cancelled) order.
SELECT c.order_id,
       CASE n.pizza_name
            WHEN 'Meatlovers'  THEN 12
            WHEN 'Vegetarian'  THEN 10
       END                                   AS base_price,
       COALESCE(e.total_extras,0)            AS extras_qty,
       CASE n.pizza_name
            WHEN 'Meatlovers'  THEN 12
            WHEN 'Vegetarian'  THEN 10
       END + COALESCE(e.total_extras,0)      AS order_revenue
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS c
JOIN pizza_names                 AS n USING (pizza_id)
LEFT JOIN (
      SELECT order_id,
             SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
      FROM pizza_get_extras
      GROUP BY order_id
) AS e USING (order_id)
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders   AS r USING (order_id)
WHERE r.cancellation IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL – sum up every order’s revenue to obtain Pizza Runner’s total earnings.
SELECT SUM(
           CASE n.pizza_name
                WHEN 'Meatlovers' THEN 12
                WHEN 'Vegetarian' THEN 10
           END
           + COALESCE(e.total_extras,0)
          ) AS total_revenue
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS c
JOIN pizza_names                 AS n USING (pizza_id)
LEFT JOIN (
      SELECT order_id,
             SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
      FROM pizza_get_extras
      GROUP BY order_id
) AS e USING (order_id)
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders   AS r USING (order_id)
WHERE r.cancellation IS NULL;
```

Running the last query yields the exact figure for “total_revenue”, i.e. the total amount of money Pizza Runner has earned after excluding cancelled orders and adding $1 for every extra topping.
